  "description": "WICZUD crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 41 c d. Reported CIF formula moiety: C42 H98 O15 Sm4 Ti1. From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Ti1 (Ti) has 5 O neighbors; Sm2D (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Sm1D (Sm) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.488-5.342 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 84.07-163.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Sm4Ti(μ5-O)(μ3-OPri)2(μ-OPri)6(OPri)6]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ5-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
